<Component>
	<Description>
		IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN
			Der Masseanschluss, auch "Masse" , "Ground"  "GND" oder "GNDREF" genannt (englisch fuer "ground reference")
			Jede Schaltung benötigt mindestens einen solchen Masseanschluss, denn er legt die verbundene Node auf Null Volt fest, und berechnet dann die anderen Spannungen in Abhängigkeit
			zu dieser Node.
			(Ohne einen Masseanschluss wird die Simulationsrechnung fehlschlagen und eine Fehlermeldung ausgeben, denn der Simulator weiss dann nicht, auf welcher Höhe die Spannungen berechnet werden sollen) 
		
			Meistens wird er mit dem "Minus" Anschluss der Spannungsquelle verbunden.
		ELSE
			The Ground reference, also called "ground","GND" or "GNDREF".
			Every circuit needs at least one of this to have a voltage reference, because it defines the connected node to be zero Volt.
			(without a ground node, the simulation will fail and throw an error message, because then the simulator doesn't know at which heights the voltages are.)
						
			Usually it is connected to the "minus" connection of the supplying voltage source.
		ENDIF
	</Description>
	<qucs_sch>
		GND [name] [active] [xpos] [ypos] [xtext] [ytext] [mirrorx] [rotate]
	</qucs_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		gndref // no specific value for ground nodes needed.
	</Default_Values>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L anicad:0
		F 0 "[name]"
		F 1 "[value]"
		F 2 "[footprint]"
		F 3 "[datasheet]"
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Spice>
		[n] connect 0 // defines the connection to the only pin , called [n] , to the Ground node, called 0.
	</Spice>
	<qucs_symbol>
		<Line 0 0 0 10 #000080 2 1>
		<Line -11 10 22 0 #000080 2 1>
		<Line -7 16 14 0 #000080 2 1>
		<Line -3 22 6 0 #000080 2 1>
		<.PortSym 0 0 [n] 0>
	</qucs_symbol>
	<eeschema_symbol>
		DRAW
		P 6 0 1 0 0 0 0 -50 50 -50 0 -100 -50 -50 0 -50 N
		X n 1 0 0 0 D 50 50 1 1 W N
		ENDDRAW
	</eeschema_symbol>
	<purchase>
        <link>
		    <url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fo%2Ferdungsbaender-6140350.html</url>
			<title>IF [language] EQUAL_TO "de" THENUebersicht ErdungELSEOverview of groundingENDIF</title>
			<detail>IF [language] EQUAL_TO "de" THENVerschiedene Massnahmen zur Erdung, wie Erdungsbaender oder Erdungsstangen bei Conrad ElectronicELSEVarious measures for grounding, such as flat bands or grounding rodsENDIF</detail>
		</link>
	</purchase>
</Component>

<Component>
	<Description>
		IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN
			Eine Spannungsquelle. Eine Quelle von elektrischer Energie.
			Diese Komponente kann als einfache dc Quelle verwendet werden, aber auch als sinus-wellen-Quelle, als Pulsierte Quelle, als Dreiecksquelle oder als Sägezahnquelle.
			Welche dieser Quellentypen verwendet wird, hängt von dem eingegebenen Wert ab.
			
			Alle Quellentypen haben unterschiedliche Parameter, siehe Beispielliste.
			Aber sie haben alle auch einen gemeinsamen, aber optionalen Parameter: Die Nominal-Leistung Pn darf beschrieben werden, darf aber auch weggelassen werden.
			Wenn sie gegeben wird, beispielsweise durch ein Statement wie Pn=20W , dann wird ein blaues Diagramm links von der Quelle dargestellt.
			Dieses Diagramm wird eine Animation anzeigen, welche die aktuellen Leistungen relativ zu der gegebenen Nominal-Leistung darstellt.
			Sie müssen allerdings den Animationen-Schalter (auf der linken Seite des Programms) einschalten, um Animationen zu nutzen.
		ELSE
			A voltage source. An electric power supply.
			This component can be used as a simple dc source, but can also be a sine wave source, a pulsed source, a triangle-shaped or a sawtooth-shaped source.
			Which one of these source types is used, depends on the given value.
				
			All source types have different parameters, see in the examples.
			But they all have one optional parameter: The nominal power p_nom may be given but it may also be omitted.
			If it is given, for example in a statement as Pn=20W , then a blue chart area is displayed left of the source.
			That chart will show an animation that displays the actual power relative to the given nominal power.
			You must switch on the animations handler (on the left side of the program) to use the animations.
		ENDIF
	</Description>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L anicad:VSOURCE
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		3.3V // A dc voltage supply with 3,3V.
		type=dc v_dc=3.3V Pn=10W // a dc voltage supply with 3,3V and a nominal Power of 10 Watt
		type=sin amplitude=325V freq=50Hz // a sine wave with 325V peak (equals 230V effective value) and a frequency of 50 Hertz.
		type=sin amplitude=325V freq=50Hz Pn=3kW //a sine wave with 325V amplitude and a frequency of 50 Hertz, and a nominal Power of 3000 Watt.
		type=sin amplitude=325V freq=50Hz v_offset=0V t_delay=0.0s theta=0 phase=0 // a sine wave voltage with further parameters. Described in chapter "4.1.2 Sinusoidal "Source of the ngspice user manual at ngspice.sourceforge.io/docs/ngspice-39-manual.pdf
		type=pulse v_high=5.0V t_high=2ms t_low=1ms // A pulsed power supply, delivering a PWM signal of 5.0V 
		type=pulse v_high=5.0V t_high=2ms t_period=3ms // The same pulsed power supply but with different time parameters.
		type=pulse v_low=0V v_high=9V t_delay=0.5ms t_rise=10ms t_fall=12ms t_high=20ms t_low=10ms // A pulsed power supply which has a rise time and a fall time, to create a PWM signal with voltage-"ramps".
		type=triangle v_low=0V v_high=9V t_delay=0.5ms t_rise=100us t_fall=110.5us // triangle voltage source 
		type=sawtooth v_low=0V v_high=7.2V t_delay=0 t_rise=1.5ms // sawtooth voltage source
		type=pwl tv=(0ms 3V 2ms 3V 2.1ms 5V 5ms 5V 7ms 3V ) // a piece wise linear voltage source, with time-voltage pairs given. See at chapter 4.1.4 "Pice-Wise Linear" in the ngspice handbook
		type=pwl tv=(0ms 3V 2ms 3V 2.1ms 5V 5ms 5V 7ms 3V ) r=2ms td=1.5ms // a pwl voltage source with repetition and start delay.
	</Default_Values>
	<eeschema_symbol>
		// -- signal types --
		DEFINE [type] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:type IN:[value]
		
		// -- signal type dc --
		IF  [type] STARTS_WITH dc THEN
			DEFINE [v_dc] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:v_dc IN:[value]
			DEFINE [v_dc] AS_NUMBER OF:[v_dc]
		ELSE
		// - dc type by just a voltage value -
			DEFINE [v_dc] AS_NUMBER OF:[value]
			IF [v_dc] THEN 
				DEFINE [type] dc
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		
		// -- signal type sine --
		IF[type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
			DEFINE [amplitude] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:amplitude IN:[value]
			DEFINE [amplitude] AS_NUMBER OF:[amplitude]
			
			DEFINE [freq] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:freq IN:[value]
			DEFINE [freq] AS_NUMBER OF:[freq]
			
			DEFINE [v_offset] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:v_offset IN:[value]
			DEFINE [v_offset] AS_NUMBER OF:[v_offset]
			IF ![v_offset] THEN 
				DEFINE [v_offset] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
			IF ![t_delay] THEN 
				DEFINE [t_delay] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [theta] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:theta IN:[value]
			DEFINE [theta] AS_NUMBER OF:[theta]
			IF ![theta] THEN 
				DEFINE [theta] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [phase] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:phase IN:[value]
			DEFINE [phase] AS_NUMBER OF:[phase]
			IF ![phase] THEN 
				DEFINE [phase] 0
			ENDIF	
		ENDIF

		// -- signal type pulse (as in chapter 4.1.1) and forms derived from that (triangle and sawtooth forms are just pulses with different parameters) --
		IF[type] STARTS_WITH pulse  || [type] STARTS_WITH tria || [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
			DEFINE [v_low] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:v_low IN:[value]
			DEFINE [v_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[v_low]
			IF ![v_low] THEN
				DEFINE [v_low] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [v_high] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:v_high IN:[value]
			DEFINE [v_high] AS_NUMBER OF:[v_high]
		
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
			IF ![t_delay] THEN
				DEFINE [t_delay] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_rise] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_rise IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_rise] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_rise]
			IF ![t_rise] THEN
				DEFINE [t_rise] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_fall] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_fall IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_fall] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_fall]
			IF ![t_fall] THEN
				DEFINE [t_fall] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_period] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_period IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_period] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_period]	
			
			// pulse specific:
			IF [type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_high IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_high]
								
				// either t_low or t_period needed. If t_low is given, t_period is calculated:
				DEFINE [t_low] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_low IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_low]
					
			ENDIF
			// triangle specific:
			IF [type] STARTS_WITH tria THEN
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[t_rise] AND:0.001
				DEFINE [t_low]  AS_MATH_MUL OF:[t_fall] AND:0.001
			ENDIF
			// sawtooth specific:
			IF [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[t_rise] AND:0.001
				DEFINE [t_low] [t_high] 999999
			ENDIF
			
			
			IF ![t_period] THEN
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_rise] AND:[t_fall]
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_period] AND: [t_high]
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_period] AND: [t_low]
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [nr_pulses] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:nr_pulses IN:[value]
			DEFINE [nr_pulses] AS_NUMBER OF:[nr_pulses]
		ENDIF
		// -- signal type pwl (as in chapter 4.1.4)
		
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN 
			DEFINE [tv] AS_SUBTEXT AFTER:(BEFORE:)OF:[value]
			DEFINE [r] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r IN:[value]
			DEFINE [td] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:td IN:[value]
			
			DEFINE [r] AS_NUMBER OF:[r]
			DEFINE [td] AS_NUMBER OF:[td]
		ENDIF
		
		// ---- power parameters ----
		DEFINE [p_nom] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:Pn IN:[value]
		DEFINE [p_nom] AS_NUMBER OF:[p_nom]
		IF [p_nom] THEN 
			DEFINE [red] 0
			DEFINE [green] 0
		ENDIF
		// ---- general drawing for all ----
		DRAW
		IF [value] CONTAINS squaresymbol THEN
			S -200 -200 200 200 0 1 0 N
		ELSE
			C 0 0 200 0 1 0 N
			<Line 0 -200 0 400 #A0A0A0 2 1> // line indicating voltage source type
			// red "+" symbol out of two lines:
			//    x    y  dx dy  color 
			<Line 30 -240 40 0  #FF0000 2 1>
			<Line 50 -260  0 40 #FF0000 2 1>
			// blue "-" symbol out of one line:
			<Line 30  240 40 0  #0000FF 2 1>
		ENDIF
			
		// --- connections for all ----
		X npos 1 0 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 I
		X nneg 2 0 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 I
		// --- power drawing ---
		IF [p_nom] THEN
			<Rectangle  -210 200 -30 -400      #000080 2 1 #000080 1 1> // blue background rectangle
		ENDIF
		// ---- type specific drawing ----
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH dc THEN
			<Text 0  0 80 #0000F0 0 "[v_dc]IF[spice_primitive]THEN[spice_primitive]ELSEVENDIF">
			<Line -100 -50 200 0 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -70   50 140 0 #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
			<Line -150 50  50  0    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -100 50  0   -100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -100 -50 100 0    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 0    -50 0   100  #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 0    50  100 0    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 100  50  0  -100  #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 100  -50 50 0     #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
				A -60 0 60 1800 0 0 1 0 N 100 100 100 100
				A  60 0 60 0 -1800 0 1 0 N 100 -100 100 100
				//<Earc -120 0 180  180 120 70 #0000F0 2 1 2 1 0>
				//<Earc 0    0 180 -180 120 70 #0000F0 2 1 2 1 0>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN
			<Text 0 0 80 #0000F0 0 "PWL">
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH tria THEN	
			<Line -150 50  100  -100    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -50 -50  100   100    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line  50  50  100  -100    #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
		   //Line  x     y  dx    dy  color    
			<Line -160  50  120  -100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line  -40 -50    0   100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line  -40  50  120  -100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line   80 -50    0   100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line   80  50   60  -50  #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		
		ENDDRAW
		
	</eeschema_symbol>
	<animation>
		IF [p_nom] THEN
			DEFINE [i_act] I[npos]
			DEFINE [v_act] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[npos] AND:V[nneg]
			DEFINE [p_act] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[i_act] AND:[v_act]
			DEFINE [p_act] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[p_act]
			
			DEFINE [share] AS_MATH_DIV       OF:[p_act] AND:[p_nom]
			DEFINE [share] AS_MATH_MUL       OF:[share] AND: 100
			IF ![share] THEN DEFINE [share] -1 ENDIF

			// - define the parameters of the display rectangle (color from green to red, and the height) -
			IF [share] EQUAL_OR_HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN	
				IF [share] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN 100 THEN
					DEFINE [red] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[share] AND:2.55
					DEFINE [red] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[red]
					DEFINE [green] AS_MATH_SUB OF:255 AND:[red]
				ELSE 
					DEFINE [red] 255
					DEFINE [green] 0
				ENDIF
				DEFINE [red]   AS_HEXADECIMAL_FORMAT OF:[red]   LENGTH:2      // makes 0-> 00,  108 -> 6C , 253 -> FF
				DEFINE [green] AS_HEXADECIMAL_FORMAT OF:[green]	LENGTH:2		// green value 
				DEFINE [color] #[red][green]00					// color format #RrGgBb

				DEFINE [height] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[share] AND:4	
				DEFINE [height] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[height]
				DEFINE [number] AS_DECIMAL_FORMAT OF:[share] FORM:###.#
				// - draw it: -
				<Rectangle  -215 200 -20 -[height] [color] 2 1 [color] 1 1> // red or yellow or green foreground rectangle
				T 0         -245 -225 70 0 0 P:[number]%               // number of p_act / p_nom in Percent. Can be >100 but not <0.
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
	</animation>
	<Spice>
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH dc THEN
			V_[individual] [npos] [nneg] DC [v_dc]
		ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
				IF [amplitude] && [freq] THEN
					V_[individual] [npos] [nneg] SIN([v_offset] [amplitude] [freq] [t_delay] [theta] [phase])
				ELSE
					 <Dialog title="missing value for voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
						The sine wave voltage source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
						This component needs at least an amplitude and a frequency to define a sine wave.
						But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
						amplitude in Volt=[amplitude] 
						frequency in Hertz=[freq]
						Please enter a correct value.
					</Dialog>
				ENDIF
			ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
					IF [v_low] && [v_high] && [t_rise] && [t_fall] && [t_high] && [t_period] THEN
						V_[individual] [npos] [nneg] PULSE([v_low] [v_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period] IF[nr_pulses]THEN[nr_pulses]ENDIF)
					ELSE
						<Dialog title="missing value for voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
							The pulsed voltage source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
							This component needs at least an the voltage and and the time durations to define how long it is high and low.
							But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
							high value in Volt=[v_high] 
							high time in seconds=[t_high]
							rise time in seconds=[t_rise]
							fall time in seconds=[t_fall]
							period in seconds=[t_period]
							Please enter a correct value.
						</Dialog>
					ENDIF
				ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH tria THEN
						IF [v_low] && [v_high] && [t_rise] && [t_fall] THEN
							V_[individual] [npos] [nneg] PULSE([v_low] [v_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period] IF[nr_pulses]THEN[nr_pulses]ENDIF)

						ELSE
							<Dialog title="missing value for triangle shaped voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
								The triangle voltage source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
								This component needs at least an the voltage and and the time durations to define how long it shall rise and how long it shall fall.
								But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
								high value in Volt=[v_high] 
								rise time in seconds=[t_rise]
								fall time in seconds=[t_fall]
								period in seconds=[t_period]
								Please enter a correct value.
							</Dialog> 
						ENDIF
					ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
							IF [v_low] && [v_high] && [t_rise] THEN
								V_[individual] [npos] [nneg] PULSE([v_low] [v_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period] IF[nr_pulses]THEN[nr_pulses]ENDIF)
							ELSE
							<Dialog title="missing value for voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
								The sawtooth-shaped voltage source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
								This component needs at least the voltage and and the time durations to define how long it shall rise.
								But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
								high value in Volt=[v_high] 
								rise time in seconds=[t_rise]
								period in seconds=[t_period]
								Please enter a correct value.
							</Dialog>
							ENDIF
						ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN 
								IF [tv] THEN
									V_[individual] [npos] [nneg] PWL([tv]) IF[r]THENr=[r]ENDIF IF[td]THENtd=[td]ENDIF
								ELSE
									<Dialog title="missing value for pwl voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150">
										The piece-wise linear (pwl) voltage source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]":
										It needs the pairs of voltages and times in the tv parameter. 
										Please make sure, that these tv pairs are surrounded by brackets ( and ) ,
										and that all values are separated correctly by a space character.
										
										You might want to check the ngspice user manual chapter 4.1.4 "Piece-Wise Linear" for details.
									</Dialog>							
								ENDIF
							ENDIF
						ENDIF
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
	</Spice>
	<purchase>
			<link>
				<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fo%2Ffunktionsgeneratoren-1100100.html</url>
				<title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Uebersicht Funktionsgeneratoren ELSE Overview function generatorsENDIF</title>
				<detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Eine Auswahl an Funktionsgeneratoren bei Conrad Electronic. Darunter eine Beschreibung. ELSE A collection of function generators at Conrad Electronic.ENDIF</detail>
			</link>
			<link>
				<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fnetzgeraete-und-netzteile-37349.html</url>
				<title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Uebersicht Netzteile ELSE Voltage supplyENDIF</title>
				<detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Eine Auswahl an Netzteilen bei Conrad Electronic. Darunter eine Beschreibung. ELSE A collection of voltage supply components of various types at Conrad Electronic.ENDIF</detail>
			</link>
			IF [v_dc] THEN
				<link>
					<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fp%2Fbasetech-bt-305-labornetzgeraet-einstellbar-0-30-v-dc-0-5-a-150-w-anzahl-ausgaenge-1-x-513812.html</url>
					<title>IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Labornetzgeraet 0-30V ELSE Variable voltage supply 0-30VENDIF</title>
					<detail>IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Ein einstellbares Gleichspannungs-Netzteil mit einer Ausgangsspannung von 0 bis 30 V bei Conrad Electronic. ELSE A voltage supply with a settable output voltage between 0 and 30V.ENDIF</detail>
				</link>
			ENDIF
	</purchase>
</Component>


<Component>
	<Description>
		IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN
			Eine Stromquelle. Eine Quelle von elektrischer Energie.
			Diese Komponente kann als einfache dc Quelle verwendet werden, aber auch als sinus-wellen-Quelle, als Pulsierte Quelle, als Dreiecksquelle oder als Sägezahnquelle.
			Welche dieser Quellentypen verwendet wird, hängt von dem gegebenen Wert ab.
			
			Alle Quellentypen haben unterschiedliche Parameter, siehe Beispielliste.
			Aber sie haben alle auch einen gemeinsamen, aber optionalen Parameter: Die Nominal-Leistung p_nom darf beschrieben werden, darf aber auch weggelassen werden.
			Wenn sie gegeben wird, beispielsweise durch ein Statement wie p_nom=20W , dann wird ein blaues Diagramm links von der Quelle dargestellt.
			Dieses Diagramm wird eine Animation anzeigen, welche die aktuellen Leistungen relativ zu der gegebenen Nominal-Leistung darstellt.
			Sie müssen allerdings den Animationen-Schalter (auf der linken Seite des Programms) einschalten, um Animationen zu nutzen.
		ELSE
			A current source. An electric power supply.
			This component can be used as a simple dc source, but can also be a sine wave source, a pulsed source, a triangle-shaped or a sawtooth-shaped source.
			Which one of these source types is used, depends on the given value.
			
			
			All source types have different parameters, see in the examples.
			But they all have one optional parameter: The nominal power p_nom may be given but it may also be omitted.
			If it is given, for example in a statement as p_nom=20W , then a blue chart area is displayed left of the source.
			That chart will show an animation that displays the actual power relative to the given nominal power.
			You must switch on the animations handler (on the left side of the program) to use the animations.
		ENDIF
	</Description>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L anicad:ISOURCE
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		1.4 // A dc current supply with 1,4 Ampere.
		type=dc i_dc=1.4 p_nom=10W // a dc current supply with 1.4A and a nominal Power of 10 Watt
		type=sin amplitude=100m freq=500Hz // a sine wave with 0.1 A amplitude and a frequency of 500 Hertz.
		type=sin amplitude=100m freq=500Hz p_nom=10W //a sine wave with 0.1 A amplitude and a frequency of 500 Hertz, and a nominal Power of 10 Watt.
		type=sin amplitude=2 freq=500Hz i_offset=0 t_delay=0.0s theta=0 phase=0 // a sine wave current supply with 2 ampere amplitude, a frequency of 500 Hertz and further parameters described in chapter "4.1.2 Sinusoidal "Source of the ngspice user manual at ngspice.sourceforge.io/docs/ngspice-39-manual.pdf
		type=pulse i_high=1.5 t_high=20ms t_low=10ms // A pulsed power supply, delivering a PWM signal of 1.5 A 
		type=pulse i_high=1.5 t_high=20ms t_period=30ms // The same pulsed power supply but with different time parameters.
		type=pulse i_low=0 i_high=9 t_delay=1.5ms t_rise=10ms t_fall=12ms t_high=20ms t_low=10ms // A pulsed power supply which has a rise time and a fall time, to create a PWM signal with current-"ramps".
		type=triangle i_low=0 i_high=9 t_delay=1.5ms t_rise=10us t_fall=11.5us // triangle current source 
		type=sawtooth i_low=0 i_high=7.2 t_delay=0 t_rise=1.5ms // sawtooth current source
		type=pwl ti=(0ms 3 2ms 3 2.1ms 5 5ms 5 7ms 3 ) // a piece wise linear current source, with time-current pairs given as ti. See at chapter 4.1.4 "Pice-Wise Linear" in the ngspice handbook
		type=pwl ti=(0ms 3 2ms 3 2.1ms 5 5ms 5 7ms 3 ) r=2ms td=1.5ms // a pwl current source with repetition and start delay.
	</Default_Values>
	<eeschema_symbol>
	
		// -- signal types --
		DEFINE [val_noa] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:ATO:OF:[value] // Removes all "A" characters from the value, to avoid Ampere being misinterpreted as "atto"
		
		DEFINE [type] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:type IN:[val_noa]
		
		// -- signal type dc --
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH dc THEN
			DEFINE [i_dc] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:i_dc IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [i_dc] AS_NUMBER OF:[i_dc]
		ELSE
		// - dc type by just a voltage value -
			DEFINE [i_dc] AS_NUMBER OF:[val_noa]
			IF [i_dc] THEN 
				DEFINE [type] dc
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		// -- signal type sine --
		IF[type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
			DEFINE [amplitude] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:amplitude IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [amplitude] AS_NUMBER OF:[amplitude]
			
			DEFINE [freq] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:freq IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [freq] AS_NUMBER OF:[freq]
			
			DEFINE [i_offset] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:i_offset IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [i_offset] AS_NUMBER OF:[i_offset]
			IF ![i_offset] THEN 
				DEFINE [i_offset] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
			IF ![t_delay] THEN 
				DEFINE [t_delay] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [theta] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:theta IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [theta] AS_NUMBER OF:[theta]
			IF ![theta] THEN 
				DEFINE [theta] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [phase] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:phase IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [phase] AS_NUMBER OF:[phase]
			IF ![phase] THEN 
				DEFINE [phase] 0
			ENDIF
			
		ENDIF
		
		// -- signal type pulse (as in chapter 4.1.1) --
		IF[type] STARTS_WITH pulse  || [type] STARTS_WITH tria || [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
			DEFINE [i_low] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:i_low IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [i_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[i_low]
			IF ![i_low] THEN
				DEFINE [i_low] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [i_high] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:i_high IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [i_high] AS_NUMBER OF:[i_high]
		
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
			IF ![t_delay] THEN
				DEFINE [t_delay] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_rise] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_rise IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [t_rise] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_rise]
			IF ![t_rise] THEN
				DEFINE [t_rise] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_fall] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_fall IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [t_fall] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_fall]
			IF ![t_fall] THEN
				DEFINE [t_fall] 0
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_period] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_period IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [t_period] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_period]	
			
			// pulse specific:
			IF [type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_high IN:[val_noa]
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_high]
								
				// either t_low or t_period needed. If t_low is given, t_period is calculated:
				DEFINE [t_low] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_low IN:[val_noa]
				DEFINE [t_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_low]
					
			ENDIF
			// triangle specific:
			IF [type] STARTS_WITH tria THEN
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[t_rise] AND:0.001
				DEFINE [t_low]  AS_MATH_MUL OF:[t_fall] AND:0.001
			ENDIF
			// sawtooth specific:
			IF [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
				DEFINE [t_high] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[t_rise] AND:0.001
				DEFINE [t_low] [t_high] 999999
			ENDIF
			
			
			IF ![t_period] THEN
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_rise] AND:[t_fall]
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_period] AND: [t_high]
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_period] AND: [t_low]
			ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [nr_pulses] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:nr_pulses IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [nr_pulses] AS_NUMBER OF:[nr_pulses]
		ENDIF
			// -- signal type pwl (as in chapter 4.1.4)
		
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN 
			DEFINE [ti] AS_SUBTEXT AFTER:(BEFORE:)OF:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [r] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r IN:[val_noa]
			DEFINE [td] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:td IN:[val_noa]
			
			DEFINE [r] AS_NUMBER OF:[r]
			DEFINE [td] AS_NUMBER OF:[td]
		ENDIF
			
		// ---- power parameters ----
		DEFINE [p_nom] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:p_nom IN:[val_noa]
		DEFINE [p_nom] AS_NUMBER OF:[p_nom]
		IF [p_nom] THEN 
			DEFINE [red] 0
			DEFINE [green] 0
		ENDIF
		// ---- general drawing for all ----
		DRAW
		IF [value] CONTAINS squaresymbol THEN
			S -200 -200 200 200 0 1 0 N
		ELSE
			C 0 0 200 0 1 0 N
			<Line -200 0 400 0 #A0A0A0 2 1> // line indicating current source type
			// red "+" symbol out of two lines:
			//    x    y  dx dy  color 
			<Line 30 -240 40 0  #FF0000 2 1>
			<Line 50 -260  0 40 #FF0000 2 1>
			// blue "-" symbol out of one line:
			<Line 30  240 40 0  #0000FF 2 1>
		ENDIF

		// --- connections for all ----
		X npos 1 0 300 100 D 50 50 1 1 I
		X nneg 2 0 -300 100 U 50 50 1 1 I
		// --- power drawing ---
		IF [p_nom] THEN
			<Rectangle  -210 200 -30 -400      #000080 2 1 #000080 1 1> // blue background rectangle
		ENDIF
		// ---- type specific drawing ----
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH dc THEN
			<Text 0  0 80 #0000F0 0 "[i_dc]IF[spice_primitive]THEN[spice_primitive]ELSEAENDIF">
			<Line -100 -50 200 0 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -70   50 140 0 #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
			<Line -150 50  50  0    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -100 50  0   -100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -100 -50 100 0    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 0    -50 0   100  #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 0    50  100 0    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 100  50  0  -100  #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line 100  -50 50 0     #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN
			<Text 0 0 80 #0000F0 0 "PWL">
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
				A -60 0 60 1800 0 0 1 0 N 100 100 100 100
				A  60 0 60 0 -1800 0 1 0 N 100 -100 100 100
				//<Earc -120 0 180  180 120 70 #0000F0 2 1 2 1 0>
				//<Earc 0    0 180 -180 120 70 #0000F0 2 1 2 1 0>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH tria THEN	
			<Line -150 50  100  -100    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line -50 -50  100   100    #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line  50  50  100  -100    #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
		   //Line  x     y  dx    dy  color    
			<Line -160  50  120  -100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line  -40 -50    0   100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line  -40  50  120  -100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line   80 -50    0   100 #0000F0 2 1>
			<Line   80  50   60  -50  #0000F0 2 1>
		ENDIF
		
		ENDDRAW
		
	</eeschema_symbol>
	
	<animation>
		IF [p_nom] THEN
			DEFINE [i_act] I[npos]
			DEFINE [v_act] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[npos] AND:V[nneg]
			DEFINE [p_act] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[i_act] AND:[v_act]
			DEFINE [p_act] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[p_act]
			
			DEFINE [share] AS_MATH_DIV       OF:[p_act] AND:[p_nom]
			DEFINE [share] AS_MATH_MUL       OF:[share] AND: 100
			

			// - define the parameters of the display rectangle (color from green to red, and the height) -
			IF [share] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN 100 THEN
				DEFINE [red] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[share] AND:2.55
				DEFINE [red] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[red]
				DEFINE [green] AS_MATH_SUB OF:255 AND:[red]
			ELSE 
				DEFINE [red] 255
				DEFINE [green] 0
			ENDIF
			DEFINE [red]   AS_HEXADECIMAL_FORMAT OF:[red]   LENGTH:2      // makes 0-> 00,  108 -> 6C , 253 -> FF
			DEFINE [green] AS_HEXADECIMAL_FORMAT OF:[green]	LENGTH:2		// green value 
			DEFINE [color] #[red][green]00					// color format #RrGgBb

			DEFINE [height] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[share] AND:4	
			DEFINE [height] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[height]
			DEFINE [number] AS_DECIMAL_FORMAT OF:[share] FORM:###.#
			// - draw it: -
			<Rectangle  -215 200 -20 -[height] [color] 2 1 [color] 1 1> // red or yellow or green foreground rectangle
			T 0         -245 -225 70 0 0 P:[number]%               // number of p_act / p_nom in Percent. Can be >100 but not <0.
		ENDIF
	</animation>
	<Spice>
		IF [type] STARTS_WITH dc THEN
			I_[individual] [nneg] [npos] DC [i_dc]
		ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
				IF [amplitude] && [freq] THEN
					I_[individual] [npos] [nneg] SIN([i_offset] [amplitude] [freq] [t_delay] [theta] [phase])
				ELSE
					 <Dialog title="missing value for voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
						The sine wave current source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
						This component needs at least an amplitude and a frequency to define a sine wave.
						But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
						amplitude in Ampere=[amplitude] 
						frequency in Hertz=[freq]
						Please enter a correct value.
					</Dialog>
				ENDIF
			ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
					IF [i_low] && [i_high] && [t_rise] && [t_fall] && [t_high] && [t_period] THEN
						I_[individual] [nneg] [npos] PULSE([i_low] [i_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period] IF[nr_pulses]THEN[nr_pulses]ENDIF)
					ELSE
						<Dialog title="missing value for current source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
							The pulsed current source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
							This component needs at least the current value and and the time durations to define how long it is high and low.
							But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
							high value in Ampere=[i_high] 
							high time in seconds=[t_high]
							rise time in seconds=[t_rise]
							fall time in seconds=[t_fall]
							period in seconds=[t_period]
							Please enter a correct value.
						</Dialog>
					ENDIF
				ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH tria THEN
						IF [i_low] && [i_high] && [t_rise] && [t_fall] THEN
							I_[individual] [nneg] [npos] PULSE([i_low] [i_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period] IF[nr_pulses]THEN[nr_pulses]ENDIF)

						ELSE
							<Dialog title="missing value for triangle shaped voltage source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
								The triangle current source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
								This component needs at least an the current and and the time durations to define how long it shall rise and how long it shall fall.
								But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
								high value in Ampere=[i_high] 
								rise time in seconds=[t_rise]
								fall time in seconds=[t_fall]
								period in seconds=[t_period]
								Please enter a correct value.
							</Dialog> 
						ENDIF
					ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH saw THEN
							IF [i_low] && [i_high] && [t_rise] THEN
								I_[individual] [nneg] [npos] PULSE([i_low] [i_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period] IF[nr_pulses]THEN[nr_pulses]ENDIF)
							ELSE
							<Dialog title="missing value for current source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
								The sawtooth-shaped current source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
								This component needs at least the current and and the time durations to define how long it shall rise.
								But at least one of these parameters is not defined correctly:
								high value in Ampere=[i_high] 
								rise time in seconds=[t_rise]
								period in seconds=[t_period]
								Please enter a correct value.
							</Dialog>
							ENDIF
						ELSEIF [type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN 
								IF [ti] THEN
									I_[individual] [nneg] [npos] PWL([ti]) IF[r]THENr=[r]ENDIF IF[td]THENtd=[td]ENDIF
								ELSE
									<Dialog title="missing value for pwl current source named [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150">
										The piece-wise linear (pwl) source named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]":
										It needs the pairs of voltages and times in the ti parameter. 
										Please make sure, that these ti pairs are surrounded by brackets ( and ) ,
										and that all values are separated correctly by a space character.
										
										You might want to check the ngspice user manual chapter 4.1.4 "Piece-Wise Linear" for details.
									</Dialog>							
								ENDIF
							ENDIF
						ENDIF
					ENDIF
				ENDIF
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
	</Spice>
	<purchase>
			<link>
				<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fo%2Ffunktionsgeneratoren-1100100.html</url>
				<title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Uebersicht Funktionsgeneratoren ELSE Overview function generatorsENDIF</title>
				<detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Eine Auswahl an Funktionsgeneratoren bei Conrad Electronic. Darunter eine Beschreibung. ELSE A collection of function generators at Conrad Electronic.ENDIF</detail>
			</link>
			<link>
				<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fnetzgeraete-und-netzteile-37349.html</url>
				<title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Uebersicht Netzteile ELSE Voltage supplyENDIF</title>
				<detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Eine Auswahl an Netzteilen bei Conrad Electronic. Darunter eine Beschreibung. ELSE A collection of voltage supply components of various types at Conrad Electronic.ENDIF</detail>
			</link>
			IF [v_dc] THEN
				<link>
					<url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fp%2Fbasetech-bt-305-labornetzgeraet-einstellbar-0-30-v-dc-0-5-a-150-w-anzahl-ausgaenge-1-x-513812.html</url>
					<title>IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Labornetzgeraet 0-30V ELSE Variable voltage supply 0-30VENDIF</title>
					<detail>IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Ein einstellbares Gleichspannungs-Netzteil mit einer Ausgangsspannung von 0 bis 30 V bei Conrad Electronic. ELSE A voltage supply with a settable output voltage between 0 and 30V.ENDIF</detail>
				</link>
			ENDIF
	</purchase>
</Component>

<Component>
	<Description>
		IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Ein Widerstand. 
		Mit einem Wert in der Einheit Ohm. 
		ELSE A Resistor.
		With a value in the unit Ohm.
		ENDIF
	</Description>
	<eeschema_sch>
		L pspice:R
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
        100 // Resistor with 100 Ohm. 
		1.5k  // Resistor with 1500 Ohm 
		1,5k  // Resistor with 1500 Ohm (using a comma is possible but a point is recommended.)
		2.2e4 // Resistor with 2.2x10^4=22 000 Ohm = 22 Kilo Ohm 
		1M  // Resistor value with 1 <u>Mega</u>Ohm = 1 Million Ohm
		1m  // Resistor value with 1 <b>Milli</b>Ohm<br> 
		//+= 1/1000 Ohm = 0,001 Ohm
    </Default_Values>
	<Spice>
        DEFINE [ohm] AS_NUMBER OF:[value]
        IF [ohm] THEN
            // DEFINE [value] AS_NULL
        ELSE
            <Dialog title="missing ohm value for [name]" type="error" dimension="450x100"> 
                The resistor named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
                Please enter a number at that place.
            </Dialog>
        ENDIF
        R_[name] [pin1] [pin2] [ohm]
	</Spice>
	<purchase>
        <link>
            <url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fo%2Fmosfets-5104021.htmlhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fwiderstaende-17441.html</url>
            <title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO "de" THEN Uebersicht WiderstaendeELSEOverview of resistorsENDIF</title>
			<detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO "de" THEN Auswahl an Widerstaenden verschiedener Bauformen bei Conrad Electronic ELSECollection of resistors of different types at Conrad ElectronicENDIF</detail>
        </link>
        <link>
            <url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fpotentiometer-17440.html</url>
           <title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO "de" THEN Uebersicht PotentiometerELSEOverview of potentiometersENDIF</title>
			<detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO "de" THEN Auswahl an Potentiometern verschiedener Bauformen bei Conrad Electronic ELSECollection of potentiometers of different types at Conrad ElectronicENDIF</detail>
        </link>
	</purchase>
    <eeschema_symbol>
		
		(rectangle (start -1.016 3.81) (end 1.016 -3.81)
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default) (color 0 0 0 0))
		  (fill (type none))
		)

		(pin passive line (at 0 6.35 270) (length 2.54)
		  (name "~" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)
