<Component>
<Description>
IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN Eine Spule, auch Inductor genannt.
	Es gibt zwei Möglichkeiten, diese Spule zu beschreiben:
	
	Option A: Einfach den Wert in Henry eingeben. Zum Beispiel 22m oder 22mH
	
	Option B: Eine Spule mit ohmschem Serienwiderstand:
	Ein Wert wie "henry=1m ohm=20m" mit einem integrierten Serienwiderstand is realistischer, denn echte Spulen haben etwas Widerstand.
	Der Draht aus dem die Spule besteht ist nie perfekt und hat etwas Widerstand. Und die Anschluss-pins haben auch immer etwas Widerstand.
	(Ausserdem ist ein gewisser Widerstand gut für die Stabilitat der Simulationsrechnung, denn es hilft dem Simulationsprogramm die Ströme zu berechnen, wenn der Widerstand grösser als null ist. Das vermeidet Divisionen durch null.)
ELSE A coil, also called inductor.
	There are two ways to describe this component:

	Option A: Just write the value in Henry. For example 22m or 22mH

	Option B: a coil with ohmic series resistance:
    a value such as "henry=1m ohm=20m" with an internal series resistance is more realistic, because real coils have some resistance.
	The wire of which the coil consists of, is never perfect and has some resistance. And also the connection pins always have some resistance.
	(Also some series resistance is good for the stability of the circuit simulation, it helps the simulator program to calculate currents when the resistance larger than zero. That avoids division by zero.)
ENDIF
</Description>	
<eeschema_sch>
    L pspice:INDUCTOR
    F 0 "[name]"
    F 1 "[value]"
    F 2 "[footprint]"
    F 3 "[datasheet]"
</eeschema_sch>
<Default_Values>
	22mH // ideal coil with 22mH
	henry=22m symbol=iec // ideal coil with 22mH and the rectangular iec type symbol.
	henry=1m ohm=20m // non-ideal but realistic coil with inductance of 1mH and an internal series resistance of 20 milli Ohm.
</Default_Values>
<Spice>
    DEFINE [datasheet] asset.conrad.com/media10/add/160267/c1/-/en/001385270DS01/datasheet/1385270-wuerth-elektronik-we-fcl-744866223-line-choke-22-mh-200-m-25-a-1-pcs.pdf
    DEFINE [henry] AS_NUMBER OF:[value]
	IF [iniamp] THEN DEFINE [iniamp] AS_NUMBER OF:[iniamp] ENDIF
	
    IF [henry] THEN
        L_[name] [1] [2] [henry] IF [iniamp] THENIC=[iniamp]ENDIF 
    ELSE
        DEFINE [henry] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:henry IN:[value]
        DEFINE [henry] AS_NUMBER OF:[henry]
        
        DEFINE [ohm] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:ohm IN:[value]
        DEFINE [ohm] AS_NUMBER OF:[ohm]
        
        DEFINE [volt] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:volt IN:[value]
        DEFINE [volt] AS_NUMBER OF:[volt]
        
        IF [henry] || [ohm] || [volt] THEN
    
    // ---- model ----
    .subckt coil_[individual] pos neg
        //coil                          
        IF[henry] THEN L_[individual] pos IF [ohm] THEN high ELSEIF [volt] THEN low ELSE neg ENDIF ENDIF [henry] ENDIF
        //induction resistance             |<---- positive connection ---->| |<--- negative connection --->|
        IF[ohm]THEN R_[individual] IF[henry]THEN high ELSE pos ENDIF IF[volt]THEN low ELSE neg ENDIF [ohm] ENDIF
        //inducing dc voltage:              |<---- positive connection --------------------------------->|
        IF[volt]THEN V_[individual] IF[ohm] THEN low ELSEIF [henry] THEN high ELSE pos ENDIF ENDIF neg DC [volt] ENDIF
    .ends
        // ---- component ----
    X_coil_[individual] [1] [2] coil_[individual]
        
        ELSE
            <Dialog title="missing Henry value for coil [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
            The coil is simulated as an inductor by default. But the coil named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
            This component expects an L value in Henry. 
            Please enter a number at that place, or a text such as "henry=20m ohm=0.3"
            </Dialog>
        ENDIF
    ENDIF 
</Spice>
