<Component>
	<Description>
		IF [language] EQUAL_TO de THEN
			Ein Kondensator.
			Er hat den eingegebenen Wert in Farad.
			
			Info für Experten:
			Er hat auch einen kleinen Serienwiderstand mit 1 milliOhm und einen grossen Paralellwiderstand mit 1MegaOhm.
			In den meisten Schaltungen haben diese beiden Widerstände keine Wirkung, und Sie können sie ignorieren.
			Sie wurden eingefügt, um die Simulationsstabilität sicherzustellen - und es ist ein bisschen realistischer, 
			denn die Kontaktstellen eines Kondensators haben üblicherweise einen Kontaktwiderstand in Serie zum Bauteil, und 
			Paralell existiert stets ein Parasitärwiderstand, weil das Material zwischen den Kondensatorplatten einen endlichen Widerstand hat.
		
			Aber falls Sie diese Widerstände entfernen und einen idealen Kondensator ohne jegliches parasitäres Element haben wollen,
			können Sie ein Statement hinzufügen wie r_s=-1 r_p=-1 (oder einen anderen Wert kleiner als 0).
			In diesem Fall liegt es jedoch an Ihnen, die Simulationsstabilität sicherzustellen und es ist empfohlen das ngspice user manual zu lesen. 
			
			Natürlich können Sie für die Widerstände auch jeden beliebigen Wert eintragen.
			Zum Beispiel wenn Sie schlecht verlötete Kontaktstellen mit 3,3 Ohm simulieren
			möchten, können Sie eintragen r_s=3.3
			
			Das symbol lässt sich zu einem Elektrolytkondensator "Elko" ändern mit symbol=elko 
		ELSE
			A Capacitor. 
			It has the given value in Farad.
			
			Expert info:
			It also has a small series resistance of 1 milli Ohm and a large paralell resistance of 1 Mega Ohm.
			In most circuits, this additional resistance has no impact, and you can ignore it.
			That series resistance is there to ensure the simulation stability - and it is a bit more realistic,
			because every capacitor has some parasitic resistance.
			
			But if you want to remove that series resistance and get an ideal capacitor without any parasitic element, 
			you can write a statement such as r_s=-1 r_p=-1 (or any other value smaller than zero).
			In that case, it is your own duty to ensure the simulation stability and reading the ngspice user manual is advised.
			
			Of course you can also define any other value for these two resistances.
			For example if you want to simulate badly soldered contacts with 3.3 Ohm,
			you can insert r_s=3.3 
			
			
		ENDIF
	</Description>

	<eeschema_sch>
		L pspice:C
	</eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		2.2uF // 2,2 micro Farad. The micro sign here is not µ but u
		2.2E-6 // 2,2 micro Farad. The E here means "...times ten to the power of..." so this is 2.2x10^-6F=2.2uF
		10m // 10 milli Farad.
		capacity=10mF r_s=-1 r_p=-1 // also 10mF, but the serial and paralell resistance are removed.
		capacity=10mF r_s=1mOhm r_p=100kOhm // also 10mF, but with serial and paralell resistances defined 
		capacity=0.05 symbol=elko // a capacitor with 0,05F=50mF. The symbol is marked with a + to indicate an electrolytic capacitor ("elko")
		capacity=0.05 symbol=elecrolytic // a capacitor with 0,05F=50mF. The symbol is marked with a + to indicate an electrolytic capacitor
	</Default_Values>
	<eeschema_symbol>
		DEFINE [farad] AS_NUMBER OF:[value]
		IF ![farad] THEN
			DEFINE [farad] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:capacity IN:[value]
			DEFINE [farad] AS_NUMBER OF:[farad]
			
			DEFINE [inivolt] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:inivolt IN:[value]
			DEFINE [inivolt] AS_NUMBER OF:[inivolt]
			
			DEFINE [symbol] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:symbol IN:[value]
			
			DEFINE [r_s] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_s IN:[value]
			DEFINE [r_s] AS_NUMBER OF:[r_s]
			
			DEFINE [r_p] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_p IN:[value]
			DEFINE [r_p] AS_NUMBER OF:[r_p]
		ENDIF
		
		IF ![r_s] THEN 
			DEFINE [r_s] 0.001 // low series resistance 
		ENDIF
		IF ![r_p] THEN 
			DEFINE [r_p] 1E9 // high paralell resistance
		ENDIF
		
		DRAW
			P 2 0 1 20 -80 -30 80 -30 N
			P 2 0 1 20 -80 30 80 30 N
			X ~ 1 0 150 120 D 50 50 1 1 P
			X ~ 2 0 -150 120 U 50 50 1 1 P
			IF [symbol] STARTS_WITH el THEN // elko or electrolytic etc. adds the "+"
				P 2 0 1 0 70 80  30 80 N
				P 2 0 1 0 50 100 50 60 N
			ENDIF
		ENDDRAW
	</eeschema_symbol>
	<Spice>
		IF ![farad] THEN
			<Dialog title="missing Farad value for [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
				The capacitor named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
				This component expects an C value in Farad. 
				Please enter a number at that place.
			</Dialog>
		ENDIF
		
		IF [r_s] EQUAL_OR_LOWER_THAN 0 THEN
			C_[individual] [pin1] [pin2] [farad] IF[inivolt]THENic=[inivolt]ENDIF
		ELSE
			.subckt DEVICE_CAPACITOR_[individual] 1 2
				R_s 1 mid [r_s] // series resistor
				IF [r_p] HIGHER_THAN 0 THEN
					R_p mid 2 [r_p] // paralell resistor
				ENDIF
				Cap mid 2 [farad] IF[inivolt]THENic=[inivolt]ENDIF
			.ends
			X_Capacitor_[individual] [pin1] [pin2] DEVICE_CAPACITOR_[individual]
			
		ENDIF
	</Spice>
    <purchase>
		<link>
		    <url>https://cdn.retailads.net/tc.php?t=151241C1001130856T&deeplink=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.conrad.de%2Fde%2Fc%2Fkondensatoren-17428.html</url>
		    <title>IF[language] EQUAL_TO "de" THEN Uebersicht Kondensatoren ELSE Overview of capacitors ENDIF</title>
            <detail>IF[language] EQUAL_TO "de" THEN Auswahl an Kondensatoren verschiedener Bauarten bei Conrad.de ELSE Overview of capacitors of various types at Conrad electronicENDIF</detail> 
		</link>
	</purchase>
   
</Component>


<poti_intro>
A potentiometer.

---- Value examples ----
A potentiometer has two parameters:
1. the resistance R in Ohm. That is a number larger than zero.
2. the slider position S, where S must be a value greater than zero and smaller than 1.
(It is recommended to use at least 0.01 and at most 0.99 for S values. )

-- Simple use examples --
A value "R=4.7k S=0.01" is a 4,7 kiloOhm Potentiometer, with a slider position down at 1%
and the value "R=220 S=0.99" is a 220 Ohm Potentiometer, with a slider all up at 99%.

-- advanced, time dependent examples --
- sine wave -
R=1000 s_type=sin s_mid=0.5 s_amplitude=0.49 frequency=2kHz t_delay=0ms damping=0 phase=0 
That is a Potentiometer, where the slider slides up and down in a sine wave with the parameters:
	1. R=1000 means the Ohm value is 1 kilo Ohm.
	2. s_type=sin means that the slider shall move up and down in a sine wave
	3. s_mid=0.5 means that the sinus wave shall move around the middle value 0.5
	4. s_amplitude=0.49 means that the maximal difference ("amplitude") shall be 0.49. That means it moves between 0.5-0.49=0.01 and 0.5+0.49=0.99.
	5. frequency=2kHz means that the slider shall move up and down 2000 times per second.
	(6) t_delay=0 means that there is no time delay where the slider sine wave starts.  Optional parameter, default is 0.
	(7) damping=0 means the damping factor in 1/s at which the sine waves amplitude is reduced. Optional parameter, default is 0.
	(8) phase=0 means the phase in degrees at which the sin is turned at the beginning. Optional parameter, default is 0. 
	
-- pulse example --
R=4.7k s_type=pulse s_low=0.2 s_high=0.8 t_low=1ms t_high=2ms t_rise=100us t_fall=200us t_delay=1ms
Defines a potentiometers where the slider slides up and down in a pulse between 20% and 80%:
The parameters are:
	1. R=4.7k means that the Ohm value is 4,7 kilo Ohm.
	2. s_type=pulse means that the slider value shall move up and down in a linear (pulse-like) wave.
	(3) s_low=0.2 means that the lower value of that pulse is at 20%. Optional parameter, default is 0.01=1%
	(4) s_high=0.8 means that the higher value of that pulse is at 80%. Optional parameter, default is 0,99=99%
	5. t_low=1ms means that the lower value shall be held constant for 1 millisecond
	6. t_high=2ms means that the higher value shall be held constant for 2 milliseconds
	(7) t_rise=100us means that the time for the transition from low to high shall take 100 microseconds. Optional parameter, default is zero.
	(8) t_fall=200us means that the time for the transition from high to loww shall tatke 200 microseconds. Optional parameter, default is zero.
	info: the sum of parameters 5+6+7+8 make the period time. That is how you define the frequency of the pulse. Here it is 1ms+2ms+0,1ms+0.2ms=3,3ms
	(9) t_delay=1ms means that there is 1ms delay before the slider starts moving.  Optional parameter, default is 0. 
</poti_intro>

<Component>
    <Description>
        INCLUDE poti_intro
    </Description>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L anicad:Potentiometer
        // ALIAS Device:R_POT Device:R_POT_US // commented out, because it is already in Device.alib.
    </eeschema_sch>
	<Default_Values>
		R=220k S=0.35 // A potentiometer with 220 kilo Ohm and a slider position of 35% 
		R=4.7k s_type=pulse s_low=0.2 s_high=0.8 t_low=1ms t_high=2ms t_rise=100us t_fall=200us t_delay=1ms // Slider position moving up and down
			//+<br> between 20%=0.2 and 80%=0.8 with 
			//+<br> 1ms delay, 100us rise time, 200us fall time, 1ms low time, and 2ms high time, 
			//+<br> which results in a period time of 3.3ms, because 1ms+2ms+100us+200us=3.3ms
		
		R=1000 S=SIN(0.5,0.4,2k,1m,0,0) // Slider position moving up and down in a sine wave form around 0.5 and an amplitude of 0.4 (so between 0.1 and 0.9)
			//+<br> with a frequency of 2kHz, a time delay of 1ms, 0 damping and 0 phase.
		R=1000 s_type=sin s_mid=0.5 s_amplitude=0.49 frequency=2kHz t_delay=0ms damping=0 phase=0 // Potentiometer with R=1000 Ohm= 1k Ohm.
			//+<br> Slider position moving up and down in a sine wave form around 0.5 and an amplitude of 0.49 (so between 0.01 and 0.99)
			//+<br> with a frequency of 2kHz, a time delay of 0ms (which is no delay), 0 damping and 0 phase.
    </Default_Values>
    <eeschema_symbol>
		
		DEFINE [ohm13] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:R IN:[value]
        DEFINE [ohm13] AS_NUMBER OF:[ohm13]
        
        DEFINE [share] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:S IN:[value]
  
		// ---- direct definition of the share value ----
        IF [share] CONTAINS ( && [share] CONTAINS ) && [share] CONTAINS , THEN
            DEFINE [share] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:,TO: OF:[share]
		ENDIF
		
        // -- dc slider type . constant value. --  
		IF IS_NUMBER [share] THEN
			DEFINE [s_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[share]
			DEFINE [s_high] [s_low]
            DEFINE [ohm12] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[ohm13] AND:[s_low]
            DEFINE [ohm23] AS_MATH_SUB OF:[ohm13] AND:[ohm12]
			
        ENDIF
		
		// ---- indirect definition of the share value ----
		DEFINE [s_type] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:s_type  IN:[value]
		
		// -- pulse slider type --
		IF [s_type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN 
			DEFINE [s_low] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:s_low IN:[value]
			DEFINE [s_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[s_low]
			IF ![s_low] THEN DEFINE [s_low] 0.01 ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [s_high] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:s_high IN:[value]
			DEFINE [s_high] AS_NUMBER OF:[s_high]
			IF ![s_high] THEN DEFINE [s_high] 0.99 ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [t_low] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_low IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_low] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_low]
			
			DEFINE [t_high] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_high IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_high] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_high]
			
			DEFINE [t_rise] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_rise IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_rise] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_rise]
			IF ![t_fall] THEN DEFINE [t_fall] 0 ENDIF 
			
			DEFINE [t_fall] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_fall IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_fall] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_fall]
			IF ![t_fall] THEN DEFINE [t_fall] 0 ENDIF
		
			DEFINE [t_period] AS_CALCULATION OF:[t_low]+[t_high]+[t_rise]+[t_fall]
		
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
			IF ![t_delay] THEN DEFINE [t_delay] 0 ENDIF
		
		
			//chapter4.1.1 PULSE    V1      V2        TD       TR      TF       PW       PER
			DEFINE [share] PULSE([s_low] [s_high] [t_delay] [t_rise] [t_fall] [t_high] [t_period])
		ENDIF
		// -- sine wave slider type --
		IF [s_type] STARTS_WITH sin THEN
			DEFINE [s_mid] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:s_mid IN:[value]
			DEFINE [s_mid] AS_NUMBER OF:[s_mid]
			
			DEFINE [s_amplitude] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:s_amplitude IN:[value]
			DEFINE [s_amplitude] AS_NUMBER OF:[s_amplitude]
			
			DEFINE [s_low] AS_MATH_SUB OF:[s_mid] AND:[s_amplitude]
			DEFINE [s_high] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[s_mid] AND:[s_amplitude]
			
			DEFINE [frequency] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:frequency IN:[value]
			DEFINE [frequency] AS_NUMBER OF:[frequency]
			
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[value]
			DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
			IF ![t_delay] THEN DEFINE [t_delay] 0 ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [damping] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:damping IN:[value]
			DEFINE [damping] AS_NUMBER OF:[damping]
			IF ![damping] THEN DEFINE [damping] 0 ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [phase] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:phase IN:[value]
			DEFINE [phase] AS_NUMBER OF:[phase]
			IF ![phase] THEN DEFINE [phase] 0 ENDIF
			
			DEFINE [share] SIN([s_mid] [s_amplitude] [frequency] [t_delay] [damping] [phase])
		ENDIF
		
		// -- postcheck: is share defined? and with all necessary parameters? --
		// -- check share and s_type --
		IF ![share] THEN
			IF ![s_type] THEN 
				// when neither s_type nor share is defined then the s_type missing (and share can not be calculated because of that)				
				<Dialog type="error" title="slider moving type s_type not given for potentiometer">
					The potentiometer [name] at position ([xpos] | [ypos]) misses the necessesary parameter called s_type:
					The slider position called s_type is missing in the given value. That value is:
					[value]
					
					It should either have ...
					... a constant share such as: R=1k S=0.3
					...or an s_type description such as: R=1000 s_type=sin s_mid=0.5 s_amplitude=0.4 frequency=2kHz 
					Please look at the description or the example values to find out how to enter correct values.
				</Dialog>
			ELSE
				// when s_type is defined, but share is not, then the user has typed an incorrect value of s_type
				<Dialog type="error" title="s_type parameter of potentiometer not defined correctly">
					The potentiometer [name] at position ([xpos] | [ypos]) misses a necessesary parameter:
					the slider position moving type, shortly called s_type is not defined correctly.
					It should be one either pulse or sine. But the given value [s_type] is not correct.
					
					Please look at the description or the example values to find out how to enter correct values.
				</Dialog>
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		// ---- actual drawing ----- 
		DRAW
			X ~ 1 0 -150 50 U 50 50 1 1 P
			X ~ 2 150 0 50 L 50 50 1 1 P //<-middle pin
			X ~ 3 0 150 50 D 50 50 1 1 P
			S -50 -100 50 100 0 1 10 N
			IF ![animated] THEN
				<Line 100 0 -40 0 #888888 2 1>
				<Polygon_3  70 20 70 -20 50 0 #888888 2 1 #000080 2 1>
				//P 2 0 1 0 100 0 60 0 N
				//P 4 0 1 0 45 0 90 20 90 -20 45 0 F
			ENDIF
		ENDDRAW
    </eeschema_symbol>
    <animation>
		DEFINE [act_s] AS_ACTUAL OF:x_[individual].ctrl // actual value, as saved in the spice section 
        DEFINE [midy] AS_MATH_MUL OF:[act_s] AND:-200
        DEFINE [midy] AS_MATH_SUB OF:-100 AND:[midy]
        DEFINE [midy] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[midy]
		DEFINE [arry2] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[midy] AND:20
		DEFINE [arry2] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[arry2]
		DEFINE [arry3] AS_MATH_SUB OF:[midy] AND:20
		DEFINE [arry3] AS_MATH_ROUND OF:[arry3]
         
        S 50 [midy] 100 [midy] 0 1 0 N
        S 100 0 100 [midy]  0 1 0 N
		P 3 0 1 0 50 [midy] 70 [arry2] 70 [arry3] F
    </animation>
    <Spice>	   
		IF [ohm13] && [share] THEN
		//model
			.subckt potentiometer_[individual] pin1 pin2 pin3
				Vctrl ctrl 0 [share] )
					.save v(ctrl)
					
				IF IS_NUMBER [share] THEN
					R12 pin1 pin2 [ohm12]
					R23 pin2 pin3 [ohm23]
				ELSE
					R12 pin1 pin2 R='[ohm13]*V(ctrl,0)'
					R23 pin2 pin3 R='[ohm13]*(1-V(ctrl,0))'
				ENDIF
			.ends
			//component
			x_[individual] [pin1] [pin2] [pin3] potentiometer_[individual]
		ELSE
			<Dialog type="error" title="Please enter a correct value">
				Missing ohm value or share value for the potentiometer [name] at position ([xpos] | [ypos]). 
				[value] is not a valid number, please correct that.
				Please look at the description or the example values to find out how to enter correct values.
			</Dialog>
		ENDIF
    </Spice>
</Component>

<Component>
	<Description>
        A switch. Can be turned on and off.
		Here a switch is simulated by a time dependent resistor.
		When the switch is on, it has r_on ohms (r_on is 0.1 by default)
		When the switch is off, it has r_off ohms (r_off is 1E12=1 000 000 000 000 by default)
		IF[s_type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
		---- pulse switch: ----
		a pulsed switch turns on and off regularly. Its parameters are:
			t_off defines the duration in seconds of the non-connecting status.
			t_on defines the duration in seconds of the connecting status.
		ENDIF IF[s_type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN
		---- piece-wise linear (pwl) switch ----
		A piece-wise linear switch is turned on and off at times that are defined by a list of switch times.
		You can give as many switch times as you want. Each switch time is defined by a pair of two numbers:
		The first number is the point of time, given in seconds. The second number is either 1=on or 0=off.
		For example, the following value consists of three such pairs, which are saying: at 0ms start at off, until 1.5ms stay off, by 1.6ms switch on.
		(the last statement will make the switch turn on in the middle of 1.5ms and 1.6ms, which is at 1.55ms):
		
		type=pwl times=(0ms 0 1.5ms 0 1.6ms 1)
		
		for readability, the brackets ( and ) may be omitted, and values may be separated by commas or semicolons. 
		For example, the following line does the same:
		
		type=pwl times=0ms off, 1.5ms off; 1.6ms on
		
		The times list must be the last argument of the value: if you want to define r_on r_off t_delay or t_repeat , you must
		type them BEFORE the times list. This is due to the undefined length of that list, it just goes until the end of the value text.

		Expert users are advised to read the ngspice user manual chapter 4.1.4 "Piece-Wise Linear" Voltage sources
		for further details, since this switch is controlled in the numeric simulation by a PWL Vsource. 
		ENDIF
    </Description>
	<Default_Values>
		on // a swtich that connects, and has the default on resistance of r_on=0.1 Ohm.
		off // a switch that blocks, and has the default off resistance of r_off=1E9=10^9=1 MegaOhm.
		s_type=pulse t_on=2ms t_off=1ms t_delay=3ms // a switch that repeatedly is turned on and off. starts at t_delay and is on for t_on and is off for t_off. So the period is t_on+toff. 
		s_type=pulse t_on=2ms t_off=1ms r_on=0.5 r_off=100k // a switch that turns on and off, and where on and off resistance ohm values are specified
		s_type=pwl times=0ms off; 1ms off; 1.1ms on; 3ms on; 3.1ms off // a switch that starts at off state, stays off until 1ms, switches on at 1.1ms, stays on until 3ms and switches off at 3.1ms (and then stays off).
		s_type=pwl t_repeat=5ms t_delay=0.2ms times=0ms off; 1ms off; 1.1ms on; 3ms on; 3.1ms off  // a switch that does as the previous one, but repeats this switching all 5ms
   </Default_Values>
	<eeschema_sch>
        L anicad:switch
    </eeschema_sch>
	<eeschema_symbol>
		// ---- on and off Ohm values ----
		DEFINE [r_on] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_on IN:[value]
		DEFINE [r_on] AS_NUMBER OF:[r_on]
		IF ![r_on] THEN DEFINE [r_on] 0.1 ENDIF
		
		DEFINE [r_off] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:r_off IN:[value]
		DEFINE [r_off] AS_NUMBER OF:[r_off]
		IF ![r_off] THEN DEFINE [r_off] 1E12 ENDIF
		
		//threshold for on/off symbol
        DEFINE [r_threshold] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[r_on] AND:[r_off]
        DEFINE [r_threshold] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[r_threshold] AND:2

	
		// ---- switch types ----
		// -- simple case, just on or off permanently: --
		IF [value] EQUAL_TO on || [value] EQUAL_TO ON || [value] EQUAL_TO On THEN
			DEFINE [permanent] on
			DEFINE [share] DC 1
		
		ELSE IF [value] EQUAL_TO off || [value] EQUAL_TO OFF || [value] EQUAL_TO Off THEN
				DEFINE [permanent] off
				DEFINE [share] DC 0
			ELSE
				DEFINE [permanent] AS_NULL
			ENDIF
		ENDIF
		// ---- a bit more complex case, switching changes over time ----
		IF ! [permanent] THEN
			DEFINE [s_type] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:s_type  IN:[value]
			IF [s_type] STARTS_WITH pulse THEN
					
				DEFINE [t_off] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_off IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_off] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_off]
				
				DEFINE [t_on] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_on IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_on] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_on]
				
				DEFINE [t_period] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_period IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_period] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_period]
				IF ![t_period] THEN
					DEFINE [t_period] AS_MATH_ADD OF:[t_on] AND:[t_off]
				ENDIF
				
				DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
				IF ![t_delay] THEN DEFINE [t_delay] 0 ENDIF
				
				DEFINE [share] PULSE (0 1 [t_delay] 0 0 [t_on] [t_period])
			ENDIF
			IF [s_type] STARTS_WITH pwl THEN
				DEFINE [times] AS_SUBTEXT AFTER:timesBEFORE:)OF:[value]
				DEFINE [times] AS_LOWERCASE OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:=TO: OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:(TO: OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:)TO: OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:,TO: OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:;TO: OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:offTO: 0 OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:onTO: 1 OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:s_typeTO: OF:[times]
				DEFINE [times] AS_REPLACEMENT FROM:pwlTO: OF:[times]
				
				DEFINE [t_delay] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_delay IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_delay] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_delay]
				
				DEFINE [t_repeat] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:t_repeat IN:[value]
				DEFINE [t_repeat] AS_NUMBER OF:[t_repeat]
				
				IF [times] THEN
					DEFINE [share] PWL ([times]) 
				ELSE
					<Dialog type="error">
						The times list in the switch are not correctly defined.
						
						Please correct these values.
					</Dialog>
				ENDIF
			ENDIF
		ENDIF

		//S -120 -80 120 80 0 1 0 f
		(rectangle (start -3.81 1.5) (end 3.81 -1.5)
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type background))
		)		//C -80 0 20 0 0 0 N
		(circle (center -2.032 0) (radius 0.508)
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)	
		//C 80 0 20 0 0 0 N
		(circle (center 2.032 0) (radius 0.508)
		  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		  (fill (type none))
		)	
			

		IF [permanent] THEN
			IF [permanent] EQUAL_TO off THEN
				//P 2 0 0 0 -60 5 93 46 N
				(polyline
				  (pts
					(xy 2.54 0)
					(xy -2.54 1.27)
				  )
				  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
				  (fill (type none))
				)				
			ENDIF
			IF [permanent] EQUAL_TO on THEN
				(polyline
				  (pts
					(xy 2.54 0)
					(xy -2.54 0.635)
				  )
				  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
				  (fill (type none))
				)
			ENDIF
		ELSE
			//<Line startx starty dx dy color pendwidth penstyle >
			//P 2 0 1 0 -60  5 60 30 N
			(polyline
			  (pts
				(xy 2.54 0)
				(xy -2.54 0.889)
			  )
			  (stroke (width 0) (type default))
			  (fill (type none))
			)
		ENDIF
		
		//X A1 1 -300 0 200 R 50 50 1 1 P
		(pin input line (at -7.62 0 0) (length 5.08)
		  (name "A1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)	
		//X B1 2 300 0 200 L 50 50 1 1 P    
		(pin input line (at 7.62 0 180) (length 5.08)
		  (name "B1" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		  (number "2" (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27))))
		)
		
	</eeschema_symbol>
	<animation>
        DEFINE [volt] AS_MATH_SUB OF:V[A1] AND:V[B1]
        DEFINE [amp] I[A1]
		DEFINE [ohm] AS_MATH_DIV OF:[volt] AND:[amp]
		DEFINE [ohm] AS_MATH_ABS OF:[ohm]
		
		IF [ohm] THEN
			IF [ohm] HIGHER_THAN [r_threshold] THEN 
				<Rectangle -150 -50 300 100 #880000 2 1 #000080 1 0.8>// draw a red rectangle, covering the non-animated "background" switch
				P 2 0 0 0 60 5 -93 46 N	// draw an open, non-conducting switch
			ENDIF
			IF [ohm] LOWER_THAN [r_threshold] THEN
				<Rectangle -150 -50 300 100 #008800 2 1 #000080 1 0.8>// draw a green rectangle, showing that it is connected 
				P 2 0 0 0 60 0 -95 22 N// draw a closed, conducting switch
			ENDIF
			C -80 0 20 0 0 0 N
			C 80 0 20 0 0 0 N
		ENDIF
    </animation>
	
